  │                  ISARCHY                     │
  │      Arch Linux + Hyprland, made clear       │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────╯

  1. Connect to the internet (iwctl or an Ethernet cable).
  2. Install base Arch with: archinstall
  3. Before rebooting, verify and copy into Archinstall's target:
       findmnt /mnt/archinstall
       install -d /mnt/archinstall/opt
       cp -a /usr/local/share/isarchy /mnt/archinstall/opt/isarchy
  4. Boot the installed system and, as your desktop user, run:
       /opt/isarchy/install.sh

  Advanced users may install Arch manually and run the same setup afterward.
  The setup does not partition disks or install a bootloader.
